@vshcherb Assuming my idea fixes this: 2 questions:
(1) Why did it happen in the first place? Users simply playing with the setting and forgetting to reset, or did we have some faulty build or commit which activated this setting as per a false default? Can you remember anything?
(2) I do not recollect why we would need such a setting "Hide overground objects" in the first place? It may cause more issues than it solves?

See: #2357
Turning off battery optimization for K9 fixed it for me. I'm not sure why this issue is marked as closed;
K9 doesn't request this permission automatically so this is still an active bug IMHO.
